## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design tenant-scoped progressive delivery, alignment with SRE practices, and Google-native tooling.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant rollout
- Region-aware routing
- Cloud Deploy traffic controls
- Cloud Monitoring per-tenant SLIs
- Safe rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing logic (illustrative only)
function routeRequest(req){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const region = mapTenantToRegion(tenant);
  const targetRevision = selectRevision(tenant, 'v2');
  forwardTo(region, targetRevision, req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you model SLOs per tenant?
- How would you handle tenants migrating regions or throttling during a spike?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses how a candidate combines deployment strategies, DR planning, and enforcement of security/compliance in a real GCP setup.

## Key Concepts
- Blue/Green and canary deployments with automatic rollback gates
- Cross-region DR for compute and database
- CMEK encryption for storage and Cloud SQL
- Policy-as-code and drift detection (Config Connector, OPA)
- Observability, outage handling, and compliance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code for SLO gate
async function canaryGate(metrics) {
  const latencyOk = metrics.p95 < 200;
  const errorOk = metrics.errorRate < 0.01;
  return latencyOk && errorOk;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate drift detection in CI/CD and ensure fast remediations?
- What tests would you run to validate cross-region failover without customer-visible downtime?
